{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":13763478,"ns":0,"title":"Automorphisms of the symmetric and alternating groups","extract":"In group theory, a branch of mathematics, the automorphisms and outer automorphisms of the symmetric groups and alternating groups are both standard examples of these automorphisms, and objects of study in their own right, particularly the exceptional outer automorphism of S6, the symmetric group on 6 elements.","description":"Aspect of mathematical group theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}